Z||000000||fiero_nightmare||10-20-2001||11:29 PM||||about 2 months ago i fell 25 feet and crushed the vertebrae in my lower back. so now i cant get a job yet because if i stand up for over 3 or 4 hours my back is just killing me. about a month ago i found a 84 trans am at a dealership that i happen to know the owner of so he let me work off the t/a by mowing his lawn with a riding lawnmower. on september 15th my parents loaned me the money to get a 85 fiero GT that has been sitting for 4 years. since i have wanted a fiero GT really bad for 3 years i decided to sell the T/a and fix up the fiero with the money from the t/a. here is all that has been done to it.<BR>1.both 1/4 windows<BR>2.both rear brake cables<BR>3.radio<BR>4.brand new $200 windshield<BR>5.used $200 engine (2.8)<BR>6. left tail light<BR>7. 84 shifter that i made 2 inches shorter<P>after i got almost everything done my dad decided he would put in the engine oil while i was putting the radio in. after i took it for a test drive i checked the dipstick and it looked WAY over full and my dad said he either put 4,5 or 6 quarts of oil in it so i drained the oil down until it read right in between add and full. after about 50 miles it started to KNOCK (just like the old engine). as it turns out the oil dipstick mounted lower down on the new engine so i was running it on only 1 1/2 to 2 quarts of oil. the owners of the salvage yard said i could exchange the engine for another one since they have a lot of 2.8's but i only have 30 days to do it. my dad wont let me change engines again because he said that he needs the garage and it was my fault because i am the one who drained the oil out even though he is the one who put the oil in and couldn't remember how much he put in.<P>I wasted 12 days of changing engines because I had to pull it out the top and $300 on the engine total including gaskets and seals. <P>I am so sick of everything in the world.<P>sorry for wasting board space. I just needed to vent.||||reg||1
