Z||000012||BN Boomer||10-24-2001||01:30 PM||||Glad to hear that things are starting to work out with your dad and your Fiero. Maybe you should consider a rebuilt motor so as to avoid another engine swap in the near future.<P>Sometimes you just have to appreciate what you have. Over the summer my 14 year old nephew was riding a quad, lost control, and hit a tree. He fractured 3 vertebrae and damaged his spinal cord. It now appears that he will spend the rest of his life in a wheel chair. I bet he would be thrilled to be able to stand for 3 or 4 hours at a time.||||reg||1
Z||000013||84Bill||10-25-2001||08:48 AM||||What a bummer, I really feel fortunate because the worst thing that happend to me this month was being tossed out of the house I busted my azz to get then be arrested because the police would not let me take my car. then 11 hours later being served with a BS protection from abuse order and not allowed within 1000 feet of all my stuff that includes all my cloths except whats on my back, 2 Fieros under construction  including 1 Indy, all my hand tools and power tools, my computers with all my software and records, payment books for my loans and other bills, my cell phone... basicly everything I have had for the last 3 years is out of reach including my toothbrush oh and a 2 1/2 year old daughter that I took care of (24/7) for the first 2 years of her life ands watched every 1st there was to see and a 9 year old son. Good thing I had 230 bucks left to my name to buy cloths (socks, boxers, ect.)and other basic items just to get by until payday, but after I pay the lawyer a paultry 150 bucks an hour for his services (1200 retainer) I may have enough money NEXT month to maybe get some things, that is IF before the child support of 200 a week kicks in.<BR>Yeah you have every reason to hate life but hey dont worry, things get better the older you get and so much easier to deal with  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
